in @glass

# Property: a substrate source's symbol tokens must be in their
# canonical (unicode) form per the multi-form symbol vocabulary table.
#
# THIRD INSTANCE of bilateral pattern #53 (property/fracture; promoted
# 2026-06-10). First instance: keyword/depth
# (@epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth +
# @kintsugi/fracture/keyword; 2026-06-10, 5e68df9 + d908798). Second
# instance: gate/diff-closure
# (@epistemologic/property/gate_matches_diff_closure +
# @kintsugi/fracture/gate; 2026-06-10, b8755cc + 20c5d97). This shard +
# its sibling fracture body (@kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift) are the
# THIRD instance, landing at the SYMBOL altitude (one altitude down
# from the OPERATOR altitude forward-promised at
# docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §14, which is one altitude down from
# the KEYWORD altitude of the first two instances).
#
# Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop is altitude-portable; candidate,
# surfaced 2026-06-11 at docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §14.7) gains
# its FIRST OPERATOR/SYMBOL-ALTITUDE WITNESS through this landing.
# Per #59's promotion gate: "two altitudes' worth of bilateral
# instances landed." Keyword altitude has multiple instances. Symbol
# altitude landing here is the second altitude — #59 promotes.
#
# === The multi-form symbol vocabulary table ===
#
# Engineer-typed ASCII forms auto-lift to canonical unicode at the
# substrate altitude. The table is parametric — additions extend the
# lookup, not the predicate's variant set:
#
#   engineer    canonical    notes
#   --------    ---------    -----
#   ->          →            serial propagation (bench-altitude arrow;
#                            per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1)
#   \           λ            lambda hole (Dhall/Haskell/Agda convention)
#   loop        ⟲            round-trip closure for resonators
#                            (Alex prefers `loop` over `(o)` for
#                            explicitness; canonical for resonator
#                            closure declarations)
#   _|_         ⊥            bottom / unfilled hole at substrate altitude
#   0           void         the void-document's λ₀ ground state; per
#                            shards/prism.mirror's `H = [[void-document]]`
#                            framing. NOT λ₀ — `void` is the substrate's
#                            own word. Context-gated: lift only inside
#                            inference contexts (bench / resonator /
#                            source / detector blocks per
#                            docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1); a bare
#                            integer 0 in non-inference code stays
#                            literal.
#   weighted    amplitudes   splitter port distribution at the physics-
#                            correct altitude (Reck/Clements unitary;
#                            phase + magnitude preserved). Magnitude
#                            → amplitude conversion: intensity
#                            fractions {p_i} become complex amplitudes
#                            {√p_i · e^{iφ_i}} whose squared moduli
#                            recover the fractions. The fracture body's
#                            splinter(ast) carries the elaboration at
#                            @meta/ast altitude; the lift is NOT a pure
#                            rename. Per §15 of optical-keywords.md.
#
# `<=` is NOT in the table — it is already a substrate operator at
# the type altitude (implements relation per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]) and is distinct from
# any inheritance-symbol candidate. Future additions extend the table
# without changing the predicate's shape.
#
# === Concrete vs parametric ===
#
# The predicate is parametric over the table. Each opacity surfaces
# ONE (location, engineer_form, canonical_form) triple — one offending
# token at one site, paired with its canonical replacement. The
# fracture body resolves any opacity by table lookup; no per-symbol
# variant.
#
# This is structurally distinct from the first two instances'
# per-predicate shape (`keyword_matches_depth`,
# `gate_matches_diff_closure`): the property's predicate is
# parametric over a table, not specialised per case. The bilateral
# pattern (#53) absorbs the parametric variant — the shape
# `@epistemologic/property/<X>` + `@kintsugi/fracture/<X>` carries
# both per-predicate and table-driven cases. The substrate's
# vocabulary doesn't need a new variant; this is the same pattern,
# parametric over a vocabulary table.
#
# === Verdict surface ===
#
# Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
#   success              -- every symbol token is in its canonical
#                          form per the table (or NOT in the table
#                          and therefore unaffected).
#   failure(opacity_map) -- some symbol token is in the engineer-form
#                          column when the canonical-form column is
#                          required by the substrate. Each opacity
#                          names ONE (location, engineer_form,
#                          canonical_form) triple.
#   partial(opacity_map) -- multiple symbol sites surveyed, some in
#                          canonical form and some not.
#
# Located transparency (not @glass.verdict): the kintsugi loop consumes
# the opacity_map to direct mutation. Each opacity names ONE offending
# token site; the fracture body (@kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift)
# realises the rule by lifting violations through kintsugi. The
# property names the rule; the fracture realises it; the kintsugi
# loop is the bridge.
#
# === The 0 -> void context gate ===
#
# The `0 -> void` lift is context-gated. The property's
# `is_inference_context(site)` action distinguishes inference sites
# (bench / resonator / source / detector blocks per
# docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1) from non-inference code where
# integer literal `0` stays literal. A bare `0` outside an inference
# context does NOT surface an opacity; the table lookup is gated by
# the inference-context predicate. The substrate is honest about the
# ambiguity; the resolution is structural (context), not heuristic.
#
# Other table entries (->, \, loop, _|_, weighted) are NOT
# context-gated — they have no ambiguity with literal integer code
# and lift unconditionally where they appear as symbol tokens.
#
# === Cybernetic ancestor ===
#
# Recognition #37 (`requires` IS a Paskian agreement; promoted
# 2026-06-10) names `pact` as the property-declaration form. pact
# replaces the conversation-era `grammar` keyword as the surface for
# declaring properties; the rule names `pact` directly below.
#
# Engineering ancestor: every code formatter that lifts ASCII to
# typography (Prettier's quote-style normalisation; Black's string
# canonicalisation; rustfmt's whitespace canonicalisation) names this
# discipline implicitly. The substrate's contribution is *typing* the
# vocabulary table so the kintsugi loop reads the lift directly,
# rather than the formatter inventing a per-symbol rule each time.

pact @epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form {
  # The (location, engineer_form, canonical_form) triples observed
  # in `file`. Each entry names ONE symbol token site whose engineer
  # form has a canonical equivalent per the multi-form table above.
  # Sites where the symbol is already in canonical form are NOT
  # included; the surface is the differential.
  symbol_sites(file: ref) -> [opacity] { \ }

  # Whether a site sits inside an inference context (bench /
  # resonator / source / detector block per
  # docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1). Gates the `0 -> void` lift:
  # `0` lifts only inside an inference context; outside, integer
  # literal `0` stays literal.
  is_inference_context(site: ref) -> bool { \ }

  # The canonical form for a given engineer form per the multi-form
  # table. Total function over the table's domain; partial outside
  # (returns the engineer form unchanged for non-table tokens).
  canonical_form(engineer_form: text) -> text { \ }

  # The combined property: every symbol site in `file` whose
  # engineer form has a canonical equivalent (per `canonical_form`)
  # AND, for context-gated entries, sits inside the gating context,
  # is already in its canonical form.
  # Verdict surface is transparency<p>:
  #   success              -- every applicable symbol site is
  #                          canonical.
  #   failure(opacity_map) -- some applicable symbol site is in
  #                          engineer form; each opacity names ONE
  #                          (location, engineer_form,
  #                          canonical_form) triple.
  #   partial(opacity_map) -- multiple sites, mixed verdict.
  symbol_canonical_form(file: ref) -> transparency { \ }
}

out symbol_sites
out is_inference_context
out canonical_form
out symbol_canonical_form
out @epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form
